<section class="container inspection-explainer studio-measurement" id="measurement-methods">

 <div><h2>Match the check<br/>to the feature</h2><p>Start with the drawing feature and its acceptance limits, then agree the instrument, setup and record needed for the order.</p><dl><div><dt>Dimensions &amp; fit</dt><dd>Identify mating diameters, lengths and thread requirements. Discuss suitable dimensional tools and gauges for those features.</dd></div><div><dt>Heights, profiles &amp; geometry</dt><dd>Define the datum system and the relationships between features. Confirm the setup and whether height, optical or coordinate measurement is appropriate.</dd></div><div><dt>Surface &amp; material checks</dt><dd>If roughness, coating thickness or hardness matters, state the method and acceptance criteria. Confirm which checks and records can be supplied.</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link" href="/quote/">Discuss inspection requirements</a></div>
</section>
